  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shivaji Bapurao Dhonde vs The State Of Maharashtra on 11 October, 2021 Author: Nitin W. Sambre Bench: Nitin W. Sambre 1/4 5 aba 238 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2383 of 2021 Digitally signed by Lata Lata Sunil Sunil Panjwani Panjwani Date: 2021.10.12 10:40:00 +0530 Mr. Shivaji Bapurao Dhonde ... Applicant v/s. The State of Maharashtra ...",
    "facts": "The applicant is seeking pre-arrest bail in Crime No. 538 of 2021, registered with Kurla Police Station for the offences punishable under Sections 420 and 272 of the Indian Penal Code and Sections 51,52 and 53 of the Food Safety & Standards Act, 2006. 2. The applicant had packed RBD Palmolein Oil in the packets for sale titled as Refined Sunflower Oil (Sunrish). As such it is claimed 2/4 5 aba 2383.21..doc that the applicant by misrepresenting the consumers was willing to pass on Palmolein Oil as Sunflower Oil.",
    "arguments": "The learned counsel for the applicant submits that the offences under Sections 51,52 and 53 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 is punishable with fine. According to her the entire stock is seized and that being so the custodial interrogation of the applicant is not required as the applicant was not selling the oil but only packing which is not an offence. The learned APP while opposing the bail urged that since the Analysis Report speaks of packing of RBD Palmolein Oil as refined Sunflower Oil, the necessary ingredients are made out and as such offence is registered. It is claimed that custodial interrogation of the applicant is very much warranted.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The learned counsel for the applicant submits that the offences under Sections 51,52 and 53 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 is punishable with fine. According to her the entire stock is seized and that being so the custodial interrogation of the applicant is not required as the applicant was not selling the oil but only packing which is not an offence. The learned APP while opposing the bail urged that since the Analysis Report speaks of packing of RBD Palmolein Oil as refined Sunflower Oil, the necessary ingredients are made out and as such offence is registered. It is claimed that custodial interrogation of the applicant is very much warranted.",
